cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the article."
title: "Analysis code for: maternal education, birth spacing, and under-5 mortality in 77 low- and middle-income countries"
abstract: >-
  Harmonisation and estimation code for a pooled analysis of 215 DHS and UNICEF
  MICS surveys across 79 low-income and middle-income countries, 2000-2024.
  Covers survey-weighted logistic and discrete-time survival surfaces,
  g-computation population attributable fractions under policy-eligible
  counterfactual shifts, Wagstaff decomposition of wealth-related inequality,
  and an estimand-shift decomposition benchmarking the conventional pooled
  approach. Individual-level microdata are not redistributable and are not
  included.
